# Build-time configuration for the frontend.
#
# Copy to `.env.production` — NOT `.env.local`. Vite loads `.env.local` in every
# mode including `vite dev`, which would silently point your local dev server at
# the deployed API, so a device you claimed locally would stop being recognised
# and the till would be talking to the live restaurant's data. `.env.production`
# is only read by `vite build`, which is exactly what deployment needs.
#
# In development, leave this unset: the dev server proxies /api to
# `wrangler dev`, so everything is same-origin with no CORS.

# Base URL of the deployed Worker API.
VITE_API_URL=https://restaurant-pos-api.pannuyaung.workers.dev

# There is deliberately no VITE_CURRENCY, VITE_CURRENCY_SYMBOL,
# VITE_CURRENCY_MINOR_DIGITS or VITE_TZ_OFFSET here, and adding one would be a
# mistake rather than a convenience.
#
# Those four belong to the restaurant, and the Worker's `vars` are where they
# are written down; the app reads them from `GET /auth/me` in the session
# bootstrap and holds them for the session. A build-time copy is a second source
# of truth, and the day the two disagree the screen quotes a price the bill does
# not charge. It is also the copy that is hardest to change: the Worker's value
# moves on deploy, while a value baked into the bundle moves when a tablet's
# service worker next decides to fetch a new one.
#
# Nothing renders money or a time before the caller is authenticated — the claim
# screen and the PIN screen have neither — so there is no first paint that has
# to guess.
#
# There is no VITE_APP_URL either: a device claim link is minted by the Worker
# from its own `APP_URL` var, because the admin generating one is on a different
# screen from the tablet that will open it.
